---
description: Player, enemy instances, projectiles and pools
globs:
  - src/entities/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

- `Enemy.ts` (`EnemyInstance`) and `Player.ts` are plain data plus sprite. Behavior lives in `src/ai/`; attack state machines live in `EnemyCombat.ts` and `enemyRanged/*`.
- Ranged enemy combat modules share `enemyRanged/combatPhase.ts` (`tickCooldownAndFaceTarget`, `boltToCommittedAim`, commit/interrupt). Reuse it rather than copying the cooldown or aim code.
- Projectiles and enemies are pooled. Release projectiles with `releaseProjectileSprite` (`projectilePool.ts`), and recycle enemy shells through `DefenseEnemySpawner` + `reconfigureEnemyInstance`. Reset all per-life state when an object is reused.
- Unit tests build enemies with `src/test/testEnemyInstance.ts`.
